~ map_dialogue
Zaar: So… These are the creatures that infest this cavern. They look… artificial. Like they were created with a purpose.
Aven: You have a good pair of eyes on you. These are without a doubt the servants of the Empress.
Zaar: If it is true, then you did a poor job of wiping them out. I can feel hundreds of them down below.
Aven: There was no need to "hunt them down". They cannot survive without their master.
Zaar: Why not?
Aven: Observe them closely. They have no digestive system, and so their lifespan is limited to about a week. They were a weapon, mindless, for the most part. And when she no longer needed it, she simply stopped sustaining them.
Aven: But something is not right. They lack coordination. You see, there is usually a strict chain of command, a hierarchy. But here are just simple drones. Under normal circumstances, the entire hive would be upon us, but only those in the vicinity noticed us.
Zaar: Makes our job easier if you ask me.
Aven: Certainly.
=> END